# Deployment & infrastructure
- Web app (Next.js): Vercel auto-deploys from `main`. PRs get preview deployments. No custom CI/CD.
- RunPod worker (Python): deployed as a Docker image to a RunPod serverless endpoint (RTX 4090 GPU), built and pushed manually — NOT part of the Vercel pipeline. A web-app PR does not affect the worker, and vice versa.
- Database: Neon Postgres via Vercel Marketplace (free tier). Hard limit of 10 branches per project. Preview deploys may create Neon branches that don't auto-delete — be aware of branch exhaustion.

# Platform constraints (personal-use tool)
- Neon free tier: 0.5 GB storage, 10-branch limit. Keep queries efficient.
- Vercel Hobby: 100 GB bandwidth/month. Uses Fluid Compute (no fixed function timeout ceiling; billed by CPU/memory).
- RunPod serverless: pay-per-second GPU billing. Worker efficiency matters — no unnecessary processing steps.
- Keep it simple: no microservices, no message queues, no caching layers.

# Roadmap
- Phase 1 (DONE): basic pipeline — submit URL, transcribe, view.
- Phase 2 (current): URL resolution (RSS/Apple/Spotify) + episode picker + speaker-name resolution (Claude API) + speaker rename UI.
- Phase 3: YouTube/X (yt-dlp) + batch processing + SSE progress + jobs list page.
- Phase 4: full-text search, shows grouping, voice prints, markdown download, polish, webhook hardening, stuck-job recovery.

Stay in scope — build only what the current task asks for. Update this roadmap as phases complete.
